<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica mohair prices lower at fourth winter sale.</title>
<headline>SAfrica mohair prices lower at fourth winter sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the second last mohair sale were indicative of limited demand rather than resistance to price, the Mohair Board said. Of the 1,744 bales offered 40 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2350-3400	(2380-3000)</p>
<p>		  medium     2252-2252	(2200-2250)</p>
<p>		  short	2050-2190	(2100-2210)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2350-3402	(2430-2900)</p>
<p>		  medium     2200-2300	(2200-2300)</p>
<p>		  short	2080-2372	(2200-2210)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 2750-7000	(3000-6500)</p>
<p>		  medium     2700-3300	(3000-4300)</p>
<p>		  short	2100-3302	(2200-3000)</p>
<p>The last winter sale of the season is scheduled for December 10, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
